\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Top left: CG iterations versus $h$. Top middle: the largest eigenvalue grows like $1/h$ only for the clamped face; it is exactly 1 for the free beam and for the cantilever loaded by forces. Top right: the smallest eigenvalue is constant in $h$ in every case, because the void is now thick enough. Bottom left: CG on the finest mesh ($n_H = 128$). Bottom middle: error of the compliance.}}{6}{figure.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:bc}{{8}{6}{Top left: CG iterations versus $h$. Top middle: the largest eigenvalue grows like $1/h$ only for the clamped face; it is exactly 1 for the free beam and for the cantilever loaded by forces. Top right: the smallest eigenvalue is constant in $h$ in every case, because the void is now thick enough. Bottom left: CG on the finest mesh ($n_H = 128$). Bottom middle: error of the compliance}{figure.caption.11}{}}
